# Debug-fix session (2026-09-19): the pinned SHA-256 fingerprint of the certificate that must sign
# every published release/rolling-build APK. This is a public digest, not a secret — it identifies
# the certificate, it does not grant anything. Enforced by :app:verifyReleaseSigningStability, but
# only when invoked with -PortEnforcePinnedReleaseSigning=true (release.yml only — never a plain
# local build; see PlatformGuards.signingStabilityViolations's own KDoc for the full account of why
# a checked-in keystore was rejected in favor of this file plus GitHub Actions secrets).
#
# UNSET until the operator generates the release keystore and sets the four ORT_RELEASE_* GitHub
# Actions secrets (RELEASING.md's "Signing" section has the exact keytool/gh secret set commands).
# Once that keystore exists, read its certificate's SHA-256 digest with either:
#   keytool -exportcert -keystore ort-release.keystore -alias ort-release -rfc | \
#     openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256
#   apksigner verify --print-certs app-full-debug.apk   # "Signer #1 certificate SHA-256 digest"
# and replace the single word below with that digest, lowercase, with no colons — nothing else on
# this line, and nothing else in the file needs to change.
5fdfe6d0776cea4b7d28a9d3f358473f122993e7ddc4f3378fa4e899cf3756f9
